<title>USA: Knight-Ridder Inc Q1 oper shr rises.</title>
<headline>Knight-Ridder Inc Q1 oper shr rises.</headline>
<dateline>MIAMI 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Quarter Ended	  Four Quarters Ended</p>
<p>			Mar. 30	Mar. 31    Mar. 30     Mar. 31</p>
<p>			1997	     1996	 1997	  1996</p>
<p>OPERATING REVENUE</p>
<p>Newspapers</p>
<p>Advertising</p>
<p>    Retail     $193,367	 $182,051   $833,084    $808,024</p>
<p>    General	51,498	   46,236    204,059     181,381</p>
<p>    Classified  208,516	  195,566    785,809     711,163</p>
<p>	Total     453,381	  423,853  1,822,952   1,700,568</p>
<p>  Circulation   126,855	  126,854    501,827     499,577</p>
<p>  Other	    20,594	   20,049     79,519	83,660</p>
<p> Total Newspapers 600,830	570,756  2,404,298   2,283,805</p>
<p>Business Information</p>
<p>  Services	 78,492	  126,905    352,206     491,091</p>
<p> Total Oper Rev 679,322	  697,661  2,756,504   2,774,896</p>
<p>  Net Income    174,731	   23,518    419,086     155,227</p>
<p> EPS*		  1.85	     0.24	 4.35	  1.57</p>
<p> AVG SHRS*	 94,683	   98,946     96,354	95,992</p>
<p>		    (In thousands, except share data)</p>
<p>NOTE: EPS and average shares outstanding common reflect the 2-for-1 split.</p>
<p>1997 Q1 net income above includes one-time gain of $1.36 a share on the sale of Knight-Ridder's interest in all but one of the jointly owned cable investments it had made with Tele-Communications Inc.</p>
<p>The pre-tax gain on the sale was $222 million.  After taxes, the gain was $128 million.</p>
<p>Excluding the gain, Knight-Ridder earned $0.49 in the first quarter of 1997, up $0.25 or 104.2 percent from $0.24 in the same period last year.</p>
<p>On this same basis, the company reported net income of $46.4 million, up 97.3 percent from $23.5 million last year, and operating income of $97.5 million, up 92.6 percent from $50.6 million in 1996.</p>
<p>First Call Analysts Estimates Q1 1997 $0.47.</p>
